```java
interface Greeter {
    String name();

    default String greet() {            // default: has a body
        return "Hello, " + name() + "!"; // implementers get this free
    }

    static Greeter of(String n) {       // static factory on the interface
        return () -> n;
    }
}

Greeter g = Greeter.of("Asha");
System.out.println(g.greet());          // Hello, Asha!  (no override needed)
```

```java
// Pre-Java 8: adding a new abstract method to a shipped interface...
interface Collection<E> {
    Stream<E> stream(); // if abstract, EVERY existing implementer fails to compile
}
```

```java
interface Collection<E> {
    default Stream<E> stream() {        // ships an implementation
        return StreamSupport.stream(spliterator(), false);
    }
}
// Every old class keeps compiling AND gains stream() automatically.
```
*If two implemented interfaces define the same default method, the class must override it and can pick one via `InterfaceName.super.method()`.*

```java
@FunctionalInterface
interface Calculator {
    int apply(int a, int b);            // exactly ONE abstract method
    default Calculator andThenLog() {   // default methods are fine
        return this;
    }
}

Calculator add = (a, b) -> a + b;       // lambda implements apply()
Calculator mul = (a, b) -> a * b;
System.out.println(add.apply(2, 3));    // 5
System.out.println(mul.apply(2, 3));    // 6

// Built-in example:
java.util.function.Predicate<String> isEmpty = String::isEmpty;
